From ed1338ddbda83faff5aa13b772d34a4f0a605d47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 08:30:43 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] Store the campaigns' Activity Log in the database

The Activity Log history lived in the connection manager's memory, so a
restart emptied every desk's log (#17). A campaign's lines now go to a new
table, activity_lines (campaign_id, channels, line), one row per send,
written in a session of its own and pruned to the campaign's last 500. A
desk that opens gets the last 100 addressed to its channel, as before.
Lines of a socket with no campaign stay in memory. campaign_id has no
foreign key so that writing a line never waits on a lock its handler holds
on the campaign row. init_db creates the table and adds the two character
columns the held marks use next (held_mark, taken_mark_ids).

Checked with test_ws_connect (a log that survives a new manager, pruning),
test_ws_rolls, test_campaigns, test_rest_broadcasts and test_00_startup on
a fresh database.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
